+The Linux capture reads every selected database and discovers legacy JSON under `storage/message/`.
+Any JSON source, legacy `message` row, or legacy `part` row makes the complete selected group unavailable.
+A valid root cannot hide an unsupported peer in either root order. Date filters run after capture and validation.
 
