+`session_v2`, `session_entry`, and alternative historical layouts remain unsupported.
 
-The adapter checks five metadata types against the [pinned OpenCode v1.19.5 schemas](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/810c0eba1a7348036f8bdf61e6632d0c36c6876c/packages/schema/src/session-message.ts): `agent-switched`, `model-switched`, `synthetic`, `shell`, and `compaction`. It checks required fields, types, timestamps, and source identities before it excludes these records from usage. Unknown fields, malformed shapes, and usage blocks outside the schema-defined metadata object cause refusal. That object permits arbitrary annotations, including token-like keys. Metadata still enters the duplicate check, with its complete model reference and optional metadata fields.
+Shared session token and cost columns must contain valid numeric zero values.
+The actual v2 writer leaves these aggregates at zero even when message rows report usage.
+The guard does not compare v2 sums with session totals. It never reports aggregates or uses them as fallback.
+A nonzero aggregate makes the complete group unavailable, including valid v2 usage in a mixed session.
 
-OpenCode v2 forks must resolve their parent, boundary, and sequence positions. Copied rows must match the parent's source fields after ID and session normalization. Conflicting fork metadata across roots, cycles, missing sequence columns, and unresolved boundaries cause refusal.
+Each v2 row needs a valid message ID, session ID, nonnegative sequence, and matching creation time.
+The session must exist in the same captured database. Message IDs and session sequence positions must agree across all selected roots.
+Equal canonical copies count once. Conflicting IDs or positions cause refusal. Distinct IDs with equal usage remain distinct.
+No title, timestamp, count, content match, or parent relationship establishes origin.
+
+Assistant rows require the current model, agent, content, and time fields.
+Usage requires five explicit integer counts: input, output, reasoning, cache read, and cache write.
+Missing counts, independent totals, legacy payload fields, invalid values, and incomplete observations cause refusal.
+Five explicit zeros preserve one measured zero observation. An empty source has no observation.
+
+The adapter retains strict validation for `agent-switched`, `model-switched`, `synthetic`, `shell`, and `compaction` metadata.
+The schema-defined metadata object permits arbitrary annotations. The full model reference, including its optional variant, participates in the copy check.
+Source fields stay in the canonical comparison before normalization. Session totals never establish a missing metric.
 
 The capture opens roots and descendants with Linux `openat2`. It rejects symbolic links, hard links, special files, unreadable peers, changed bytes, and changed manifests. It reads no source path through SQLite. A private SQLite VFS serves captured bytes and rejects writes, deletes, attachments, sidecars, and temporary files. Each connection uses a read-only transaction. The VFS registration, name, image descriptor, and backing bytes outlive that connection. Raw source contents remain in memory.
